A||||9||Matt88||Power Pulleys||||1||
Z||000000||Matt88||03-05-2001||11:01 PM||||Has anyone tried one of these for a V6?  It seems a fairly inexpensive means of increasing available horsepower.<P>Is there any problem with alternator, water pump, air conditioning?<P>Can the pulley be replaced in car?<P>Thanks for the help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||03-05-2001||11:09 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004771.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004771.html</A> <P>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||03-06-2001||12:30 AM||||I never drove my 3.4 without the power pulley, so I cant say if it helps performance. But the car tends to run warm and takes a while to cool back down, even at highway speeds. I don't know it there is not enough speed on the water pump or it is just my luck. Maybe some others will share their experiences too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||03-06-2001||12:52 AM||||Check out Shaun Hammits page, he has a big write up on the install and everything.  Seems like a good deal for only 80 bucks.<BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/FieroGTnos" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/FieroGTnos</A> <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||StuGood||03-06-2001||12:07 PM||||I would give this a little thought, before I did anything.  In my humble opinion, the link DXR_DAD cites above is <B>not</B> a very thorough discussion of power pulleys - and I suspect it may contain innaccurate info.  It certainly contains a lot of confusion for such a short thread...   <P>I think it's good that you are patient enough to do some research, and seek to benefit from others' experiences.  I can't offer any personal experiences - I've never used "power pulleys."           <P>FWIW, I will recommend another thread discussing power pulleys... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005979.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/005979.html</A> <BR>...of course, I like this one mostly because it has Stu's brilliant comments   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>Just as long as you keep in mind, they're just my opinions, based upon many years of nonexperience   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">!<p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 03-06-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000005||Black88GT||03-06-2001||12:19 PM||||Hmm, one of your reasons for not doing the mod is because its actual "work"?  I think that was a joke but I am not sure, I hope it was.<P>All I know is that Shaun Hammit installed his and increased his 0-60 times (6.1 -5.6,5.7) and Qtr. mile times. (14.8-14.2).  He was using NOS on these runs but the first figure was with NOS.  Also I think he said he had 2 other small mods, an intake and a TCC along with the pulley.  ||||reg||14
Z||000006||88formula||03-06-2001||07:54 PM||||I have one and I have had no problems with cooling. I thought I could feel a difference in performance but you know what people say about the ass-o-meter. It can be purely psychological.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||StuGood||03-07-2001||10:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>...All I know is that Shaun Hammit installed his and increased his 0-60 times...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Funny, I'd rather <B>decrease</B> my 0-60 time.  Just teasing - I know what you meant  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  BTW, I appreciate you being honest and complete, when you mentioned the other mods he made to his car.   <P>||||reg||12
Z||000008||Matt88||03-07-2001||04:21 PM||||Thanks for the replies.  As with many things, I was wondering if the claims for improvement are what they are advertised to be. I'll continue my plan to install one - sometime. <P>I have some experience with Chevy v8's and air-cooled VW engines. <P>Power pulleys for air-cooled VW engines work (ie, you do have more available power) but the cost is that your engine may (that is will) run quite a bit hotter - not a good thing for performance tweeked motors in the hot summer months.  Chevy V8's also have power pulleys available, however the power increase is more difficult to determine since these motors usually have lots of available torque/horsepower so a little increase is difficult to feel (ie, "ass 'o meter").||||reg||1
Z||000009||Alex4mula||03-07-2001||04:44 PM||||I have one with my 3.4 & I have no cooling problems at all. The temp runs the same as with my previous 2.8 here in hot sunny Florida (south).||||reg||1
